@tradition gerald-clinic
// Gerald clinic (FX14, 0.92.5 item 16; SW1's pitch): every cactus on the Wren is called Gerald, and they all came from Tove
// Cruz's cuttings. Every other Sunday she holds a clinic at the garden's potting bench end. Behind WEEKEND_ON.
k: 465
title: Gerald clinic
// (the user, 2026-10-25: spread across weeks, two new a weekend; was: every 2 weeks sunday week 2 from day 1)
when: every 4 weeks sunday week 2 from day 1
at: 14:30-15:15
min: 20
jitter: 10
where: 3 pool garden
hold: 1
who: cruz-tove always, janssen-hugo always, esposito-yara always, alvarez-luca always, walsh-esme always, gardener 50%, garden-lover 30%, everyone 5%
anim: water
host: cruz-tove
from: cruz-tove

== mail
- Gerald clinic tomorrow at {time}, the garden. Bring your Gerald. Mm. Or come and get one. They're very easy. Mostly.

== ask
- Gerald clinic later. Mine's leaning. Cruz says it's thinking.   #funny
- Bring your cactus to the garden this afternoon. Cruz checks every one.
- No Gerald yet? Cruz hands them out at the clinic. They're all called Gerald.   #funny

== here
- This one's thirsty. Just a sip. Mm. Good.
- Mine's got a new spike. I'm far too proud of it.   #funny
- Same pot, bigger Gerald. That's growth.   #funny

== thanks
- You join the line at the potting bench. Cruz turns each little cactus over in their hands, murmurs to it, and sends it home with a sip of water.

== chatter
- My Gerald passed the clinic. Cruz said "mm". That's a pass.   #funny
- There are more cacti called Gerald on the Wren than people now. Probably.   #funny
- I didn't have a Gerald. Now I've got one. It's on my shelf, looking pleased.   #warm
